
*.pyc

test.py

# raw_data is regenerable by the scrapers and far too large to track (the CafeF PDF archive
# alone is ~1.7 GB per ticker) — with ONE exception, opened up at the bottom of this file:
# raw_data/cafef/financials/. Git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded,
# so the path is opened one level at a time rather than with a bare `raw_data/`.
raw_data/*
!raw_data/cafef/
raw_data/cafef/*
!raw_data/cafef/financials/

# the DeepDoc DB detector weights for the onnx OCR engine (~4.7 MB). Fetched on first use from
# HuggingFace (InfiniFlow/deepdoc) by onnx_ocr.ensure_det_model; the vendored *.py detection code
# in src/web_scraper/_deepdoc/ IS tracked, only the model binary is not.
src/web_scraper/models/*.onnx
# and the VietOCR checkpoint (90 MB), which `find_vietocr_weights` also looks for here.
# ⚠️ The recogniser's CONFIG in the same directory (vietocr_vgg_seq2seq.yml, 3 KB) IS
# tracked on purpose: without it every onnx layer fetches it from vocr.vn on every
# Predictor build, and an unreachable host turns the cascade into tesseract (`VCR-1`).
src/web_scraper/models/*.pth
# and the Vietnamese language model for the two tesseract layers (vie.traineddata, 12.4 MB),
# which `find_tessdata` looks for here before falling back to this machine's own tessdata dir.
# ⚠️ The ENGINE needs no file: pymupdf statically embeds Tesseract (measured in the manylinux
# wheel as well as here), so this data file is the whole tesseract half of a Kaggle payload.
src/web_scraper/models/*.traineddata

bronze_data/

silver_data/

gold_data/

